---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/02-11/',official='https://www.suss.com/en/products-solutions/coating-solutions/coating-and-developing/acs200-gen3',spec='https://clara.nz/docs/learning/inseto/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/suss_microtec_coater_acs200-gen3.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="ACS200 Gen3 dry wafer handling" subtitle="" wide={true} description="Track dry virtual wafers through a cassette, transfer arm and chuck without process recipes."><script is:inline>window.waferTrace=import('/equipment/02-11/handling.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="drytrace"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/02-11/">← Equipment 02-11</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#wa-ref">References</a><a href="#wa-proof">Verification</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">02-11 / DRY HANDLING WITNESS</p><h2>Three wafers in. Two dry jobs out.</h2><p class="eq-lede">Cancel the middle wafer and step through the cassette, transport and chuck poses on an ACS200 Gen3. The other two wafers return to their exact original slots. No material state is changed.</p></header>
<div class="cols"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / WORK BAY</p><h3>SUSS ACS200 Gen3 · dry view</h3><div id="wa-view" aria-label="Metric ACS200 with inspection bay, cassette and chuck"></div><small id="wa-model" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</small><div class="tools"><button id="wa-whole">Whole enclosure</button><button id="wa-bay">Cassette and transport</button><button id="wa-chuck">Chuck close-up</button><button id="wa-cover">Hide shield for inspection</button></div><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The exterior panel and STEP key are live scene controls. Removing the shield is an inspection display mode, not a physical door or hardware-interlock instruction.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / DRY QUEUE</p><h3>Dispatch original identities</h3><div class="tools"><button id="wa-skip">Cancel middle job</button><button id="wa-reset">Reset queue</button></div><label>Middle wafer size<select id="wa-size"><option value="200">200 mm · same fixture</option><option value="150">150 mm · reject in 200 mm setup</option></select></label><div class="tools"><button class="run" id="wa-advance">Advance one pose</button><button id="wa-run">Complete dry batch</button></div><p id="wa-status" role="status">Dry example queue loaded.</p><p>Only one wafer can be in transit. Step to see pickup, chuck seating and return. The 150 mm wafer is a teaching mismatch for this installed cassette/chuck; the platform can take another size with a different tooling configuration.</p></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / PROVENANCE</p><h3>Keep the original slot visible</h3><p id="wa-result" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Wafer ID</th><th>Origin slot</th><th>Diameter (mm)</th><th>Status</th><th>Current location</th><th>Dry revision</th></tr></thead><tbody id="wa-rows"></tbody></table></div><div class="tools"><button id="wa-save">Export dry batch ledger JSON</button><a href={p+'example-batch.json'}>Example completed ledger</a></div></section>
<section id="wa-ref"><p class="eq-meta">04 / DOCUMENTED VARIANT</p><h3>Gen3, non-TE, with a 200 mm cassette/chuck</h3><p>The <a href={official}>SUSS product page and front oblique photograph</a> establish the rectangular enclosure, side windows, operator panel and support for 100–200 mm wafers under tooling variants. The <a href={spec}>maker’s ACS200 Gen3 brochure, V3 footprint table</a> gives 1,850 × 1,500 mm for one configuration. Asset floor extents and the 200 mm discs/chuck were checked. The ~2.17 m cabinet height, local packing, marker travel, cassette geometry and accessory placement are inferred. Original reconstruction; no manufacturer photographs republished.</p><div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'acs200.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Bounds and VR action targets</a><a href={p+'handling.mjs'}>Dry transfer state model</a></div></section>
<section id="wa-proof"><p class="eq-meta">05 / VERIFICATION &amp; SCOPE</p><h3>Identity is independent of pose</h3><p>The finite-state model advances queued → on-arm → on-chuck → completed at origin. Cancelling a job before dispatch changes no wafer location or dry revision. Size mismatch rejects the job in its original slot and the queue advances. The three scene positions are illustrative station landmarks, not a continuously solved or collision-validated robot path.</p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Independent reference case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Computed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Cancel DRY-W02, execute other two</th><td>Dry revisions 1, 0, 1; A/01, A/02, A/03 intact</td><td>Exact match</td></tr><tr><th>150 mm wafer in present 200 mm fixture</th><td>Reject in A/02, dry revision 0; A/03 completes</td><td>Exact match</td></tr><tr><th>Single wafer mid-cycle</th><td>Only active wafer changes pose; others stay in slots</td><td>Exact match</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The <code>bts.dry-wafer-ledger.v1</code> output records stable IDs, original and current slot, fixture diameter and per-event history in metre/mm units. A revision counts dry handling, not a coating. No film thickness, chemical process, spin/bake parameters, utility setup, service operation or real hardware control. Named metric anchors expose an adapter for a VR workshop; this browser view does not verify a headset session.</p></section>
</article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/02-11/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#drytrace .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.16fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.8rem}#drytrace section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}#drytrace .cols section{margin:0}#drytrace .eq-meta{margin:0}#drytrace h3{margin:.3rem 0 .6rem;font-size:1.5rem}#drytrace .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.46rem;align-items:center;margin:.65rem 0}#drytrace label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}#drytrace button,#drytrace select{min-height:40px;padding:.38rem;max-width:100%;font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--panel,transparent);color:var(--text)}#drytrace button{cursor:pointer}#drytrace button.run{background:#365e52;color:white}#drytrace button:disabled,#drytrace select:disabled{opacity:.5}#wa-view{height:clamp(269px,31vw,410px);background:#263539}#wa-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#drytrace .over{overflow:auto}#drytrace table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}#drytrace th,#drytrace td{text-align:left;padding:.44rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#wa-result{font-weight:bold}#drytrace code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:760px){#drytrace .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}#drytrace section{padding:.68rem}}
</style>
